// Part 23 of the human harness (HUMAN_CONTROLLER builds, build_controller.bat; included by human_test.cpp after
// combat_test.inc): the controllers' base, C_HumanController (game/human_controller.cpp), against the original's. Each
// side has its own controller object (the port's class with its real vtable; the original's 0xC0 bytes made by its
// own constructor, its vtable the original's), the port's copied into the original's layout before each call and the
// two compared field by field after it, with the messages each queued. The human is part 20's and 21's; what the
// controller calls outside itself is faked on both sides alike (logged, answers scripted).
//
// Part 23a: the life cycle (the constructor, Attach, Detach, the deaths), the small virtuals, the move flags, the
// inventory requests and the messages.
